    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Hermitian.20Matrix.20with.20Complex.20Entries.20has.20Real.20Diagonal/near/592626110\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=RCLike.is_real_TFAE#doc\">docs#RCLike.is_real_TFAE</a><br>\nI think we should add convenient dot notation <code>IsSelfAdjoint.re_eq</code>/<code>IsSelfAdjoint.im_eq</code>/<code>IsSelfAdjoint.rclikeRe_eq</code>/<code>IsSelfAdjoint.rclikeIm_eq</code> and then always use the <code>IsSelfAdjoint</code> spelling. The <code>RCLike</code> file imports it, though <code>Complex</code> doesn't.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I don't understand what these dot notations are supposed to be , I'm still new when it comes to Linear Algebra in Mathlib and this seems like something out of my reach.</p>\n<p>You guys can work on this(or if you really want me to do those PRs then you would have to go into specific details and theorem statements) but it would be beneficial for me if you link PRs you open related to the above in this thread , as I have learnt plenty about mathlib by looking at PRs and going through the discussions on github.</p>\n<p>Nonetheless, I'm glad that my questions sparked further conversations and ideas.</p>",
